  "result": "`slugify(text)` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes all 13 tests (the 2 existing `capitalize` tests plus 11 new ones).\n\nIt follows your rules in this order:\n- Converts `đ`/`Đ` to `d`.\n- Strips diacritics.\n- Lowercases.\n- Turns each run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one hyphen.\n- Trims the leading hyphen.\n- Cuts to 50 characters.\n- Trims any trailing hyphen left by the cut.\n\nNon-string input is converted with `String(text)`, so `null` becomes `'null'` rather than throwing.\n\nI added the new tests to `test/strings.test.js`. They cover:\n- Basic hyphenation, collapsing runs of symbols, and trimming.\n- Vietnamese text, `đ`/`Đ`, and other Latin accents.\n- Digits.\n- Empty and symbol-only input.\n- The 50-character cut, including a cut that would otherwise end in a hyphen, and a slug of exactly 50 characters.",
